{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And he shall leave them there.</b> That he not use them on another Yom HaKippurim — thus did our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expound: the garments used on this Yom HaKippurim he shall not use on another Yom HaKippurim, as it is stated: ״והניחם שם״ — this teaches that they require גניזה (storage/sequestering). And they said that the value (מחיר) of the garments was 18 maneh, and this is the meaning of והניח״ם. And you will find further in the Yerushalmi of tractate Yoma (7:3): Rabbi Hiyya taught: ״ולבשם״ — they wear out there; there they would rot and were not fit for the coming Yom HaKippurim, end of quote. And this is an explicit allusion to their גניזה."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The text has '(משקל) [מחיר]' — 'weight' in parentheses with 'value/price' in brackets as the proposed reading; rendered as 'value (מחיר)' per the bracketed correction. The letters of והניח״ם (והניחם) with final mem = 6+5+50+10+8+40 = 119, not 18; Rabbeinu Bahya cites the 18-maneh figure from rabbinic tradition without numerical explanation here, and the translation preserves it as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:05.303569729Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}